 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "124:5-11 frames the hypocrites' question («إنكارًا واستهزاءً»). As-Sa'di's «والحث على الجهاد» (124) is cut. A book for «سورة», light for «فزادتهم إيمانا», an hourglass for «في كل عام مرة أو مرتين». No motif on «الرسول». STAGING v4: c1 (124): a town by day. Three believers on the left, three men on the right (some of the hypocrites, Al-Muyassar). A book plate on 124:4-5 (a sura revealed); the hypocrites speak on 124:7 toward the believers who are present (their question is framed by the gloss «إنكارًا واستهزاءً»; nobody speaks toward an empty side); the believers read on 124:15 under a light plate (it increased them in faith: both tafsirs, by knowing it, understanding it and acting on it) and a soft sparkle on them on 124:18 (they rejoice). c2 (125-126): the same town; the three hypocrites (those with a disease in their hearts: doubt and hypocrisy, both tafsirs) turn their backs on 125:6 (As-Sa'di: they rejected it and turned away from it); nobody fades or leaves on 125:10 (they died as disbelievers): the camera only closes on them; an hourglass on 126:6-10 (tried every year once or twice); no drought, disease or affliction is drawn (the tafsirs give different examples), and nothing is acted on the negations 126:12-16. c3 (127) is kept ambient: Al-Muyassar places their slipping away in the Messenger's own gathering («من عنده»), so staging it would make them leave an empty side that stands for him. Cover: the believers reading the sura (124:15)."
 },
